  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The structure of&nbsp; the neoprene polymer is as shown below.<br />It is obtained from chloroprene which is&nbsp;2-chloro buta-1,3-diene. It is an addition homopolymer with rubber like structure and properties.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0039_a432b02c14bf.png\" style=\"width: 395px; height: 238px;\" /></p><p>Neoprene is a polymer of chloroprene which is chemically 2- chlorobuta - 1, 3 -diene (isoprene).&nbsp;Neoprene exhibits good chemical stability and maintains flexibility over a wide temperature range.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>"
